---
/*
  About.astro — short "About" section (#about).

  Reframed in R1: brief, and it now absorbs the old Engineering section —
  what you study, your EE interests, and the kind of work you want. The
  interest areas are a restrained INLINE list (small tags), deliberately not
  a card grid, to avoid the templated look.

  All prose is yours to write; interest labels are placeholders too.
*/
import Section from "./Section.astro";

// Short, factual focus areas — replace with the real ones (no card grid).
const focus = [
  "[PLACEHOLDER: focus area]",
  "[PLACEHOLDER: focus area]",
  "[PLACEHOLDER: focus area]",
];
---

<Section id="about" title="About">
  <p>
    I'm John Jacobson, though most people call me Jack. I'm an engineering
  student in the Grainger College of Engineering at the University of
  Illinois, focused on electrical engineering.
  </p>

  <p>
    I've always chased curiosity, the need to figure out how things work,
  but the one thing I could never quite understand was electricity. Tiny,
  invisible electrons that light up the world, power our computers, and
  drive everything around us. Trying to understand it led me to build my
  own computer in middle school, and computers for my friends. It led me
  to my first CS class, to Arduinos, and to studying the physics of
  electricity and magnetism.
  </p>

  <p>
    What I love about electrical engineering is its almost magical nature.
  It lets you build what should be impossible, solving physical and
  software limitations at once to arrive at something compact and elegant
  that makes life better. To me, a device that can hold and display human
  knowledge is genuinely otherworldly.
  </p>

  <p>
    I want to keep chasing that curiosity into building the kind of products
  I grew up admiring: elegant, compact, and woven so deeply into daily life
  that people forget how much engineering is behind it all.
  </p>


  <p class="about__focus-label">Current focus</p>
  <ul class="about__focus">
    {focus.map((area) => <li>{area}</li>)}
  </ul>
</Section>

<style>
  /* The global reset (* { margin: 0 }) zeroed paragraph margins, so stacked
     paragraphs had no gap. "p + p" targets only a paragraph immediately
     preceded by another paragraph, so the first paragraph gets no extra top
     margin and each following one gets a gap. (NB: this is scoped by Astro to
     paragraphs authored in THIS component — we can't reach .section__body here
     because that wrapper lives in Section.astro and carries a different scope.)
     The focus-label below is also a <p>, but it sets the same margin-top value,
     so the result is identical whichever rule applies to it. */
  p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about__focus-label {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  /* Inline "tags" — a simple wrapping row, not cards. */
  .about__focus {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .about__focus li {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px; /* pill shape */
    padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
